  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-11), throttle (left) and stick (right) seen from behind and to the right; the stick head faces the camera, the throttle shows its right (thumb) side",
  "mappingSource": "catalog (logitech.json: X52 Pro driver map http://hacks4ros.github.io/h4r_x52_joyext/doc/doxygen/d3/d14/x52_general.html + community maps); locations cross-checked with EDRefCard bindingsData.py (https://github.com/richardbuckle/EDRefCard/blob/dev/www/scripts/bindingsData.py, SaitekX52/SaitekX52Pro: 2 = Safe/fire, 3 = button right of Safe, 4 = button right of hat, 5 = black button left of hat, 7 = throttle blue button, 8 = throttle top rotary button, 9-14 = stick base switches, RX = throttle bottom rotary, RY = top rotary) and the Logitech X52 user guide product tour https://www.logitech.com/assets/65328/x52-hotas.pdf p.3-4 (no numbered figure)",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "note": "The 3 base toggles (T1/T2, T3/T4, T5/T6) and the 3-position mode rotary are on the STICK (base and head), although the catalog part ids start with \"throttle.\"; markers are on the physical controls. POV1 (TMS) is placed on the lower thumb hat and buttons 20-23 (DMS) on the upper left hat, following EDRefCard (\"stick top hat\" = buttons, POV = the other hat); not confirmed by a Logitech figure. The three MODE parts are the positions of one rotary knob; their markers are spread along that knob. Throttle rear hat, scroll wheel and the stick trigger/pinky face away. Several throttle-side controls are only candidates: from this angle the mini-stick, slider and the E button cannot be told apart reliably.",
